{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-9c3d5e54-b6f1-48fc-bd3c-c3ee0e4fd210","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a8f81462d830b39d","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9015-l1fjvfg0/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9015-E001.md","content":"# Run comparison view (side-by-side and diff) in the Dashboard\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers the experiment comparison capability in the Dashboard:\nusers can select two or more training or pipeline runs and view their\nparameters and metrics side by side, with a diff presentation that\nhighlights which parameters and metrics changed between two selected runs.\nToday, parameters and metrics live only on per-run pages, forcing data\nscientists to compare runs in exported spreadsheets; this epic brings that\ncomparison into the platform so model promotion decisions have side-by-side\nvisibility into what changed between candidate runs.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Multi-select of two or more runs from the existing runs list in the\n  Dashboard (covering both training runs and pipeline runs).\n- A comparison view presenting each selected run's parameters and metrics\n  side by side.\n- A diff presentation of the comparison that highlights which parameters\n  and metrics differ between two selected runs.\n- Read-only aggregation of run data already accessible to the Dashboard\n  (the same per-run parameters and metrics shown on existing per-run\n  pages); no new backend data plane.\n- The comparison view is the platform's shared comparison surface: later\n  integrations (e.g. opening a comparison from the Model Registry view)\n  reuse this view and its run-selection model rather than building a\n  second one.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given the runs list, when the user selects two or more runs, then a\n  comparison view opens showing each selected run's parameters and metrics\n  side by side.\n- Given two selected runs in the comparison view, then the parameters and\n  metrics that differ between them are highlighted, and unchanged values\n  are distinguishable from changed ones.\n- Given runs of both kinds (training runs and pipeline runs), the\n  comparison works identically over both — validating that Data Science\n  Pipelines run data continues to be consumable through the surfaces the\n  Dashboard already uses (Data Science Pipelines is a passive, unchanged\n  component in this strategy).\n- Given a single selected run, then the comparison entry point is not\n  offered (comparison requires two or more runs).\n- The comparison view renders successfully for runs with differing\n  parameter/metric sets (values present on one run and absent on another\n  are shown as such, not as errors).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-1 (P0)**: Users can select two or more runs and view their\n  parameters and metrics side by side in the Dashboard — the side-by-side\n  comparison view and runs-list multi-select.\n- **HLR-3 (P1)**: Provide a run \"diff\" view that highlights which\n  parameters and metrics changed between two selected runs — the diff\n  presentation of the same comparison surface, consolidated into this epic\n  with HLR-1 (one capability, one surface, higher priority P0).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":41623,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-96ffdecdd766e6e1","agent_id":"add362e9569eaf60d","session_id":"6d4629bb-6ebf-4841-9add-2a02bfaa2227","uuid":"98ec9aef-7e18-4d9c-86c7-5687635b4669","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:09:05.017Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9015 into epics"}
