{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-9c3d5e54-b6f1-48fc-bd3c-c3ee0e4fd210","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-ada77d0ce460c798","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9015-l1fjvfg0/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9015-E002.md","content":"# Producing-run lineage on registered model versions\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers run lineage in the Model Registry: a registered model\nversion records a reference to the run that produced it, so the lineage is\npart of the registry's model-version metadata and can be used to open a\ncomparison of the producing run from registry-facing surfaces. The Model\nRegistry is the source of truth linking model versions to their training\nlineage; this epic makes the producing run a resolvable part of that\nrecord.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Define how a registered model version carries a reference to the run\n  that produced it (the architecture context documents custom properties\n  on model versions as the extension point for structured metadata; the\n  concrete mechanism is an implementation decision for the Model Registry\n  team).\n- Record the producing-run reference when a model version is registered\n  from a run, including validation that the reference resolves to a run\n  in the same project.\n- Expose the producing-run reference through the Model Registry REST API\n  so Dashboard and other clients can read it.\n- Preserve compatibility: existing registered model versions without a\n  producing-run reference remain valid, and existing registration flows\n  keep working.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a model version registered with a producing run, then the model\n  version's metadata includes a reference to that run, retrievable\n  through the Model Registry REST API.\n- Given a producing-run reference on a model version, then the reference\n  resolves to the run that produced it within the same project.\n- Given a model version registered without run information, then\n  registration succeeds and the model version remains valid (the\n  producing-run reference is optional and backward compatible).\n- The lineage reference is specified and documented precisely enough for\n  a consuming UI to resolve the run and its parameters/metrics (the\n  contract the registry-side comparison entry point builds against).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-2 (P1)**: Registered model versions link back to the run that\n  produced them — the registry-side half (lineage data recorded on model\n  versions and exposed via the REST API); the \"comparison can be opened\n  from the Model Registry\" half is delivered by the Dashboard-side\n  registry entry point.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":41623,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-96ffdecdd766e6e1","agent_id":"add362e9569eaf60d","session_id":"6d4629bb-6ebf-4841-9add-2a02bfaa2227","uuid":"3ee50c0f-bb14-4c9a-8cd1-3af53de16204","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:09:13.877Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9015 into epics"}
