rsion, then the run\n  comparison view opens with the linked run pre-selected and further runs\n  can be added to the comparison.\n- Given a model version without a producing-run reference, then the\n  registry view renders normally with the comparison entry point hidden\n  or disabled (no errors, no dead links).\n- The comparison opened from the registry behaves identically to the\n  comparison opened from the runs list (same view, same side-by-side and\n  diff behavior).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-2 (P1)**: \"...so a comparison can be opened from the Model\n  Registry\" — the Dashboard-side half of HLR-2 (registry UI entry point);\n  the lineage-on-model-versions half is delivered by the Model Registry\n  epic.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":43097,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-96ffdecdd766e6e1","agent_id":"add362e9569eaf60d","session_id":"6d4629bb-6ebf-4841-9add-2a02bfaa2227","uuid":"8848aa22-5017-4f3d-89f9-2963cee4baac","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:09:24.871Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9015 into epics"}
