aggregation of run data already accessible to the Dashboard\n51\t  (the same per-run parameters and metrics shown on existing per-run\n52\t  pages); no new backend data plane.\n53\t- The comparison view is the platform's shared comparison surface: later\n54\t  integrations (e.g. opening a comparison from the Model Registry view)\n55\t  reuse this view and its run-selection model rather than building a\n56\t  second one.\n57\t\n58\t## Acceptance Criteria\n59\t\n60\t- Given the runs list, when the user selects two or more runs, then a\n61\t  comparison view opens showing each selected run's parameters and metrics\n62\t  side by side.\n63\t- Given two selected runs in the comparison view, then the parameters and\n64\t  metrics that differ between them are highlighted, and unchanged values\n65\t  are distinguishable from changed ones.\n66\t- Given runs of both kinds (training runs and pipeline runs), the\n67\t  comparison works identically over both — validating that Data Science\n68\t  Pipelines run data continues to be consumable through the surfaces the\n69\t  Dashboard already uses (Data Science Pipelines is a passive, unchanged\n70\t  component in this strategy).\n71\t- Given a single selected run, then the comparison entry point is not\n72\t  offered (comparison requires two or more runs).\n73\t- The comparison view renders successfully for runs with differing\n74\t  parameter/metric sets (values present on one run and absent on another\n75\t  are shown as such, not as errors).\n76\t\n77\t## HLR Traceability\n78\t\n79\t- **HLR-1 (P0)**: Users can select two or more runs and view their\n80\t  parameters and metrics side by side in the Dashboard — the side-by-side\n81\t  comparison view and runs-list multi-select.\n82\t- **HLR-3 (P1)**: Provide a run \"diff\" view that highlights which\n83\t  parameters and metrics changed between two selected runs — the diff\n84\t  presentation of the same comparison surface, consolidated into this epic\n85\t  with HLR-1 (one capability, one surface, higher priority P0).\n86\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-adf30b6cd92a4b39","agent_id":"ab9f2a00c4354583f","session_id":"6d4629bb-6ebf-4841-9add-2a02bfaa2227","uuid":"b25f0834-46e1-48db-b1b4-c7b69ddc6863","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:11:51.300Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-939415219a0316c7","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9015 decomposition"}
