{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b87a0e27285d1ed3","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9015-E002\n3\ttitle: Producing-run lineage on registered model versions\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9015\n5\tcomponent: Model Registry\n6\tteam: Model Registry\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 0\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 0\n17\t  human_process_gates: 1\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 6\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Producing-run lineage on registered model versions\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic delivers run lineage in the Model Registry: a registered model\n34\tversion records a reference to the run that produced it, so the lineage is\n35\tpart of the registry's model-version metadata and can be used to open a\n36\tcomparison of the producing run from registry-facing surfaces. The Model\n37\tRegistry is the source of truth linking model versions to their training\n38\tlineage; this epic makes the producing run a resolvable part of that\n39\trecord.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Define how a registered model version carries a reference to the run\n44\t  that produced it (the architecture context documents custom properties\n45\t  on model versions as the extension point for structured metadata; the\n46\t  concrete mechanism is an implementation decision for the Model Registry\n47\t  team).\n48\t- Record the producing-run reference when a model version is registered\n49\t  from a run, including validation that the reference resolves to a run\n50\t  in the same project.\n51\t- Expose the producing-run reference through the Model Registry REST API\n52\t  so Dashboard and other clients can read it.\n53\t- Preserve compatibility: existing registered model versions without a\n54\t  producing-run reference remain valid, and existing registration flows\n55\t  keep working.\n56\t\n57\t## Acceptance Criteria\n58\t\n59\t- Given a model version registered with a producing run, then the model\n60\t  version's metadata includes a reference to that run, retrievable\n61\t  through the Model Registry REST API.\n62\t- Given a producing-run reference on a model version, then the reference\n63\t  resolves to the run that produced it within the same project.\n64\t- Given a model version registered without run information, then\n65\t  registration succeeds and the model version remains valid (the\n66\t  producing-run reference is optional and backward compatible).\n67\t- The lineage reference is specified and documented precisely enough for\n68\t  a consuming UI to resolve the run and its parameters/metrics (the\n69\t  contract the registry-side comparison entry point builds against).\n70\t\n71\t## HLR Traceability\n72\t\n73\t- **HLR-2 (P1)**: Registered model versions link back to the run that\n74\t  produced them — the registry-side half (lineage data recorded on model\n75\t  versions and exposed via the REST API); the \"comparison can be opened\n76\t  from the Model Registry\" half is delivered by the Dashboard-side\n77\t  registry entry point.\n78\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-adf30b6cd92a4b39","agent_id":"ab9f2a00c4354583f","session_id":"6d4629bb-6ebf-4841-9add-2a02bfaa2227","uuid":"0b8333bc-1029-4e55-a4f1-740c7c80a6fb","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:11:51.974Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b87a0e27285d1ed3","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9015 decomposition"}
